From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: colum <colum@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 11 Nov 2026 10:20:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dsv41: TF_DS_ENGRAM_DEDUPE=1 reads a prompt chunk's repeated
 rows once

A prompt repeats n-grams: the 2-gram columns of ordinary prose hit the same bucket row for the same token pair
at many positions (" the", " of", punctuation and a word), and code or structured text repeats more. Every
occurrence was read from disk again, though the row id (bucket offset + hash mod prime) names the same bytes.

With the switch, the read-ahead and TF_DS_ENGRAM_LEAD's readers dedupe a chunk's row ids: the distinct ids are
read once and their rows copied to the repeats, which is exact. The map is open addressing from a row id to its
row in a scratch buffer, cleared per chunk, and a chunk with no repeats takes the old path untouched (so the
switch costs one pass over the ids when it finds nothing to save). The buffers are ~7.4 MB at a 2,048-token
chunk and are allocated only with the switch on.

The round's reads and the main thread's fallback are left as they are: a round can run beside the next chunk's
read-ahead (TF_DS_ENGRAM_LEAD's readers are joined before a chunk's layers), and sharing the scratch with them
would race. Bytes are identical; only the read count changes, which `tensorfold:engram_lookup_seconds_count`
shows.

Tests: prompt.zig (dedupeIds' repeats, distinct ids and clearing; a toy host's deduped gather gives the plain
gather's bytes for a chunk with repeats and for one without; the switch's values). Not run on a pair.

---
diff --git a/zig/src/families/dsv41/engram_lead.zig b/zig/src/families/dsv41/engram_lead.zig
index 45f05cd..7064791 100644
--- a/zig/src/families/dsv41/engram_lead.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/dsv41/engram_lead.zig
@@ -100,7 +100,7 @@ fn read1(eh: *EngramHost, c: *const Config, seq: []const i32, start: usize, n: u
     }
     const timed = eh.metrics;
     const t0 = if (timed) prompt.readStamp(eh) else 0;
-    try prompt.aioGather(ring, t, eh.ahead_flat[j][0..m], eh.ahead_w[j][0 .. m * t.row_w], eh.ahead_s[j][0 .. m * t.row_s]);
+    try prompt.engramReadRows(eh, ring, t, eh.ahead_flat[j][0..m], eh.ahead_w[j][0 .. m * t.row_w], eh.ahead_s[j][0 .. m * t.row_s], true);
     if (timed) eh.reads.observe(prompt.readStamp(eh) - t0);
     engram.decodeRows(eh.ahead_w[j][0 .. m * t.row_w], eh.ahead_s[j][0 .. m * t.row_s], eh.ahead_rows[j][0 .. m * t.row_w], m, t.row_w, t.row_s, 8);
     eh.lead_ready[j] = true;
diff --git a/zig/src/families/dsv41/model.zig b/zig/src/families/dsv41/model.zig
index 038f4bf..33a54b0 100644
--- a/zig/src/families/dsv41/model.zig
+++ b/zig/src/families/dsv41/model.zig
@@ -475,6 +475,9 @@ pub const Model = struct {
                 m.eh.?.io = io;
                 m.eh.?.metrics = true;
             }
+            // TF_DS_ENGRAM_DEDUPE=1: a prompt chunk's distinct rows read once, copied to their repeats
+            if (prompt.dedupeEnabled(if (std.c.getenv("TF_DS_ENGRAM_DEDUPE")) |v| std.mem.span(v) else null))
